  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Areas of frost tonight.\n\nWarm air advection in the wake of a surface ridge tonight, will \nsupport 850 mb temperatures to climb into the upper single \ndigits Celsius tonight. However, clear skies and light winds \nacross the region will likely support frost formation to form, \nespecially for areas outside of the northern Niagara Frontier as\nthere may be enough of a gradient wind to limit the areal \nextent of the frost. This being said a Frost Advisory is in \neffect tonight for Monroe, Wayne and northern Cayuga. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...An extended period of dry and warmer weather begins \nthis afternoon and likely lasts through the week.\n\nSurface high pressure will remain anchored over the eastern US this \nweek, that coupled with a ridge of high pressure aloft will maintain \nfair weather with afternoon temperatures near or above normal.",
